id: pm-8eebb6
title: Packed npx smoke timeout rejects valid slow dependency reification
description: "The packed-release smoke hard-codes 120 seconds for every subprocess. On the current host, an isolated npx tarball install completes successfully in about 155 seconds, so both npx and npm-exec fallback are killed before the CLI runs even though the identical tarball succeeds through npx and bunx."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-04T05:31:14.304Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-04T10:14:20.664Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-04T06:43:12.373Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-04T06:43:12.373Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Fresh-runner npx dependency reification has a bounded timeout above observed valid latency; the timeout remains asserted by unit tests; the canonical packed npx plus bunx smoke completes; no subprocess becomes unbounded.
parent: pm-ygli86
resolution: "Packed validation now installs the tarball once for multi-command workflows while retaining explicit npx, pm-cli alias, bunx, and strict TypeScript consumer checks under the calibrated cold-command bound."
expected_result: "Valid npx and bunx packed installs and package, calendar, upgrade, CLI, and SDK consumer workflows complete without a false 120-second or 300-second timeout."
actual_result: The optimized focused suite passes 21 tests; the exact packed smoke and hosted Gates (smokes) rerun provide terminal timing evidence.
